{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "When you say \"total overtime hours per month for the entire workforce cannot exceed 20 hours per worker,\" do you mean the overtime cap is 20 hours per individual worker per month (so total workforce overtime is 20 times the number of workers that month), or that the sum of overtime hours across all workers in a month is capped at 20 hours total?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy clarification regarding the interpretation of the overtime cap, presenting two mutually exclusive options for one constraint."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For the regular wage, you said it is paid regardless of utilization — does that mean each worker employed in a month is paid 160 hours × 30 Yuan = 4,800 Yuan for that month even if they work fewer than 160 regular hours (e.g., because production is low)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for confirmation of a specific wage calculation policy."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "When a worker is hired or fired in a given month, does that worker count toward that month's workforce (and thus receive that month's regular wage and can work that month's overtime), or do hires/fires take effect at the start of the following month?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding the effective timing of workforce changes, which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For the backorder cost of 35 Yuan per unit, is it charged on the number of units still unfulfilled at the end of each month (i.e., the backorder balance carried into the next month), or is it charged on the total units that were backordered during the month regardless of when they are eventually fulfilled?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice between two mutually exclusive calculation methods for the backorder cost."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For the inventory holding cost of 15 Yuan per unit, is it charged on the ending inventory balance at the end of each month (including June), or only on the inventory carried into the next month (i.e., not charged on June's ending inventory)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the timing of the inventory holding cost charge, presenting two mutually exclusive options for one policy decision."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 2,
  "is_atomic": false,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Can the workforce be reduced below the initial 1,000 workers (i.e., are firings allowed)?",
    "Is there any minimum workforce level that must be maintained in any month?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains two semantically independent questions: one asking whether firings are allowed (whether the workforce can drop below 1,000) and another asking if there is a specific minimum workforce level constraint. A user could answer 'yes' to firings but 'no' to a minimum level, or vice versa, so they are distinct."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Can the workforce be increased without limit (i.e., is there any cap on the number of workers that can be hired in a month or on the total workforce size)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding workforce hiring limits. Although it mentions two specific aspects (monthly hiring cap and total size cap), they are presented as alternative definitions of the same constraint (whether there is a limit), so they constitute one semantic question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "When demand is fulfilled, is there any limit on how much of a month's demand can be satisfied by outsourced units, or can all of a month's demand (current plus backorders) be met by outsourcing if that is cheaper?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the capacity limit for outsourced units relative to monthly demand."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "When demand is fulfilled from previous-month inventory, current in-house production, and outsourced units, is there any required priority or order in which these sources must be used (e.g., must inventory be used before production, or production before outsourcing), or can the model freely choose how much to draw from each source?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the priority or flexibility of sourcing options, which constitutes one independent semantic request."
}

